Introduction
❑Image denoising removes unwanted noise from digital images.
❑Noise may occur during image capture, transmission, or storage.
❑Traditional denoising methods may remove important image
details.
❑U-Net is a CNN-based deep learning architecture.
❑It uses encoder-decoder structure with skip connections.
❑Applications include:
❑MRI Denoising
❑CT Scan Enhancement
❑Satellite Imaging
❑Low-Light Photography
4 / 21

Image Noise and Its Types
❑Gaussian Noise
❑Salt and Pepper Noise
❑Speckle Noise
❑Poisson Noise
Goal
To improve image quality and visual appearance.
5 / 21

Traditional Image Denoising Methods
1. Median Filter
❑Removes salt-and-pepper noise
❑Preserves image edges
2. Gaussian Filter
❑Smoothens Gaussian noise
❑Fast implementation
❑May blur details
3. Non-Local Means (NLM)
❑Uses patch similarity
❑Better detail preservation
